-field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/range-field#features","content":"Integrates with native forms, keyboard, pointer, and touch interaction through React Aria"},"1151":{"id":"/docs/components/range-field-31","page_id":"/docs/components/range-field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/range-field#default","content":"Minimal usage with a single value and min/max bounds."},"1152":{"id":"/docs/components/range-field-32","page_id":"/docs/components/range-field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/range-field#controlled","content":"Use `onChange` for immediate updates and `onChangeEnd` for work that should run after interaction finishes."},"1153":{"id":"/docs/components/range-field-33","page_id":"/docs/components/range-field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/range-field#disabled","content":"Use `isDisabled` when the value is visible but unavailable for interaction."},"1154":{"id":"/docs/components/range-field-34","page_id":"/docs/components/range-field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/range-field#labels","content":"Combine an input label, value label, range labels, and helper text when users need additional context."},"1155":{"id":"/docs/components/range-field-35","page_id":"/docs/components/range-field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/range-field#value-display","content":"Use `valueLabel` to show formatted values, static context, or output derived from the current slider state."},"1156":{"id":"/docs/components/range-field-36","page_id":"/docs/components/range-field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/range-field#markers","content":"Use `markers` to expose a manageable set of discrete steps for a single value."},"1157":{"id":"/docs/components/range-field-37","page_id":"/docs/components/range-field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/range-field#range","content":"Pass a `number[]` to render a range with two thumbs and step markers."},"1158":{"id":"/docs/components/range-field-38","page_id":"/docs/components/range-field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/range-field#accessible-names","content":"For a single value, prefer a visible `label`; use `aria-label` only when equivalent visible context already exists."},"1159":{"id":"/docs/components/range-field-39","page_id":"/docs/components/range-field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/range-field#accessible-names","content":"For an array, provide one descriptive `thumbLabels` entry for every value. Entries are matched by index, so keep them aligned when values are added, removed, or reordered. Describe each thumb's purpose, such as `Lower warning threshold`, rather than its current number."},"1160":{"id":"/docs/components/range-field-40","page_id":"/docs/components/range-field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/range-field#accessible-names","content":"`thumbNames` configures native form field names and does not provide accessible labels. Likewise, `valueLabel`, `minLabel`, and `maxLabel` are visual context rather than substitutes for accessible naming."},"1161":{"id":"/docs/components/range-field-41","page_id":"/docs/components/range-field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/range-field#keyboard-interaction","content":"Each thumb follows the React Aria slider keyboard model:"},"1162":{"id":"/docs/components/range-field-42","page_id":"/docs/components/range-field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/range-field#keyboard-interaction","content":"Tab and Shift+Tab move among thumbs and surrounding controls."},"1163":{"id":"/docs/components/range-field-43","page_id":"/docs/components/range-field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/range-field#keyboard-interaction","content":"Arrow Right and Arrow Up increase the focused value by `step`."},"1164":{"id":"/docs/components/range-field-44","page_id":"/docs/components/range-field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/range-field#keyboard-interaction","content":"Arrow Left and Arrow Down decrease the focused value by `step`."},"1165":{"id":"/docs/components/range-field-45","page_id":"/docs/components/range-field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/range-field#keyboard-interaction","content":"Home and End move the focused thumb to its permitted bounds."},"1166":{"id":"/docs/components/range-field-46","page_id":"/docs/components/range-field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/range-field#keyboard-interaction","content":"Page Up and Page Down make larger changes."},"1167":{"id":"/docs/components/range-field-47","page_id":"/docs/components/range-field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/range-field#keyboard-interaction","content":"Directional behavior follows the user's locale where appropriate. Pointer, touch, and keyboard interaction all use the same scale and constraints."},"1168":{"id":"/docs/components/range-field-48","page_id":"/docs/components/range-field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/range-field#keyboard-interaction","content":"Markers are decorative and hidden from the accessibility tree. Ensure the field label, thumb labels, bounds, step, and formatted values communicate all required information without relying on marker appearance."},"1169":{"id":"/docs/components/range-field-49","page_id":"/docs/components/range-field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/range-field#best-practices","content":"Use an array only when every entry has a clear, independently adjustable meaning."},"1170":{"id":"/docs/components/range-field-50","page_id":"/docs/components/range-field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/range-field#best-practices","content":"Keep `value`, `thumbLabels`, and `thumbNames` aligned by index."},"1171":{"id":"/docs/components/range-field-51","page_id":"/docs/components/range-field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/range-field#best-practices","content":"Use thumb labels that explain purpose instead of repeating the current number."},"1172":{"id":"/docs/components/range-field-52","page_id":"/docs/components/range-field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/range-field#best-practices","content":"Keep array values in a stable semantic order. If crossing or reordering thumbs would make their meaning ambiguous, enforce the appropriate ordering in product state."},"1173":{"id":"/docs/components/range-field-53","page_id":"/docs/components/range-field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/range-field#best-practices","content":"Avoid large value arrays. Every entry creates another focusable control, which increases keyboard effort and cognitive load."},"1174":{"id":"/docs/components/range-field-54","page_id":"/docs/components/range-field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/range-field#best-practices","content":"Set meaningful `minValue`, `maxValue`, and `step` values. The scale should match the precision users actually need."},"1175":{"id":"/docs/components/range-field-55","page_id":"/docs/components/range-field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/range-field#best-practices","content":"Use markers only when there are few enough steps to scan. Tiny steps across a large range can create an excessive number of DOM elements."},"1176":{"id":"/docs/components/range-field-56","page_id":"/docs/components/range-field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/range-field#best-practices","content":"Use `formatOptions` for currency, percentages, measurements, and other locale-sensitive units so values display and announce their meaning."},"1177":{"id":"/docs/components/range-field-57","page_id":"/docs/components/range-field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/range-field#best-practices","content":"Use `description` for persistent guidance and `isRequired` when a value is required."},"1178":{"id":"/docs/components/range-field-58","page_id":"/docs/components/range-field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/range-field#best-practices","content":"Use `isDisabled` when the value should remain visible but unavailable for interaction."},"1179":{"id":"/docs/components/range-field-59","page_id":"/docs/components/range-field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/range-field#best-practices","content":"Use `onChange` for lightweight immediate feedback and `onChangeEnd` for expensive requests, filtering, or calculations."},"1180":{"id":"/docs/components/range-field-60","page_id":"/docs/components/range-field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/range-field#best-practices","content":"Use a text-entry control when exact numeric input is essential. A track is best for exploring or adjusting values within known bounds."},"1181":{"id":"/docs/components/range-field-61","page_id":"/docs/components/range-field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/range-field#a-thumb-is-missing-a-label-or-form-value","content":"Check the same index in `thumbLabels` and `thumbNames`. Each array entry renders a thumb, and its accessible label and form name are read from the corresponding positions. A form name does not replace an accessible label."},"1182":{"id":"/docs/components/range-field-62","page_id":"/docs/components/range-field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/range-field#typescript-reports-the-wrong-callback-value-type","content":"Keep the controlled or default value and callback signatures consistent. When inference is unavailable, provide the generic explicitly: `<RangeField<number>>` for a scalar or `<RangeField<number[]>>` for an array."},"1183":{"id":"/docs/components/range-field-63","page_id":"/docs/components/range-field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/range-field#the-controlled-thumbs-do-not-move","content":"The `value` prop is the source of truth. Update the scalar or array in `onChange` without changing its intended shape. For arrays, return a new array so application state observes the update."},"1184":{"id":"/docs/components/range-field-64","page_id":"/docs/components/range-field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/range-field#values-snap-unexpectedly","content":"Verify that `step` represents the intended interval from `minValue`. Every thumb snaps to valid positions on the same configured scale."},"1185":{"id":"/docs/components/range-field-65","page_id":"/docs/components/range-field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/range-field#the-final-marker-is-missing","content":"Markers begin at `minValue` and appear at complete step positions. `maxValue` receives a marker only when the range is evenly divisible by `step`."},"1186":{"id":"/docs/components/range-field-66","page_id":"/docs/components/range-field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/range-field#markers-are-crowded-or-rendering-is-slow","content":"Increase `step` or omit `markers`. Large ranges with small steps can produce many decorative elements even when users cannot distinguish them visually."},"1187":{"id":"/docs/components/range-field-67","page_id":"/docs/components/range-field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/range-field#the-value-or-endpoint-labels-are-blank","content":"Enable automatic current-value output with `valueLabel={true}` or provide custom content. `minLabel` and `maxLabel` display only explicitly supplied content; neither defaults to a numeric bound or receives `formatOptions`."},"1188":{"id":"/docs/components/range-field-68","page_id":"/docs/components/range-field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/range-field#negative-values-do-not-behave-as-expected","content":"Negative values are supported. Set a negative `minValue` and ensure every scalar or array value remains within the configured bounds."},"1189":{"id":"/docs/components/range-field-69","page_id":"/docs/components/range-field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/range-field#the-range-configuration-is-invalid","content":"Provide finite bounds where `minValue` is less than `maxValue`, a finite `step` greater than zero, and finite values inside the configured range."},"1190":{"id":"/docs/components/segmented-controller","page_id":"/docs/components/segmented-controller","type":"page","content":"SegmentedController","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Components"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/segmented-controller"},"1191":{"id":"/docs/components/segmented-controller-0","page_id":"/docs/components/segmented-controller","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/segmented-controller","content":"A segmented controller is a linear set of two or more segments, each of which functions as a button. A segmented controller allows users to select options, switch views, or sort elements."},"1192":{"id":"/docs/components/segmented-controller-1","page_id":"/docs/components/segmented-controller","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/segmented-controller#installation","content":"Installation"},"1193":{"id":"/docs/components/segmented-controller-2","page_id":"/docs/components/segmented-controller","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/segmented-controller#examples","content":"Examples"},"1194":{"id":"/docs/components/segmented-controller-3","page_id":"/docs/components/segmented-controller","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/segmented-controller#default","content":"Default"},"1195":{"id":"/docs/components/segmented-controller-4","page_id":"/docs/components/segmented-controller","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/segmented-controller#controlled","content":"Controlled"},"1196":{"id":"/docs/components/segmented-controller-5","page_id":"/docs/components/segmented-controller","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/segmented-controller#sizes","content":"Sizes"},"1197":{"id":"/docs/components/segmented-controller-6","page_id":"/docs/components/segmented-controller","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/segmented-controller#icon--text","content":"Icon + Text"},"1198":{"id":"/docs/components/segmented-controller-7","page_id":"/docs/components/segmented-controller","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/segmented-controller#icon-only","content":"Icon Only"},"1199":{"id":"/docs/components/segmented-controller-8","page_id":"/docs/components/segmented-controller","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/segmented-controller#overflow","content":"Overflow"},"1200":{"id":"/docs/components/segmented-controller-9","page_id":"/docs/components/segmented-controller","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/segmented-controller#rtl-direction","content":"RTL Direction"},"1201":{"id":"/docs/components/segmented-controller-10","page_id":"/docs/components/segmented-controller","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/segmented-controller#disabled-states","content":"Disabled States"},"1202":{"id":"/docs/components/segmented-controller-11","page_id":"/docs/components/segmented-controller","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/segmented-controller#customization","content":"Customization"},"1203":{"id":"/docs/components/segmented-controller-12","page_id":"/docs/components/segmented-controller","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/segmented-controller#data-attributes","content":"Data Attributes"},"1204":{"id":"/docs/components/segmented-controller-13","page_id":"/docs/components/segmented-controller","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/segmented-controller#accessibility","content":"Accessibility"},"1205":{"id":"/docs/components/segmented-controller-14","page_id":"/docs/components/segmented-controller","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/segmented-controller#keyboard-navigation","content":"Keyboard Navigation"},"1206":{"id":"/docs/components/segmented-controller-15","page_id":"/docs/components/segmented-controller","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/segmented-controller#aria-support","content":"ARIA Support"},"1207":{"id":"/docs/components/segmented-controller-16","page_id":"/docs/components/segmented-controller","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/segmented-controller#best-practices","content":"Best Practices"},"1208":{"id":"/docs/components/segmented-controller-17","page_id":"/docs/components/segmented-controller","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/segmented-controller#when-to-use-a-segmented-controller","content":"When to Use a Segmented Controller"},"1209":{"id":"/docs/components/segmented-controller-18","page_id":"/docs/components/segmented-controller","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/segmented-controller#when-not-to-use","content":"When Not to Use"},"1210":{"id":"/docs/components/segmented-controller-19","page_id":"/docs/components/segmented-controller","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/segmented-controller#props","content":"Props"},"1211":{"id":"/docs/components/segmented-controller-20","page_id":"/docs/components/segmented-controller","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/segmented-controller#segmentedcontroller","content":"SegmentedController"},"1212":{"id":"/docs/components/segmented-controller-21","page_id":"/docs/components/segmented-controller","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/segmented-controller#segmentedcontrolleritem","content":"SegmentedControllerItem"},"1213":{"id":"/docs/components/segmented-controller-22","page_id":"/docs/components/segmented-controller","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/segmented-controller#default","content":"An uncontrolled segmented controller with a default selection. The component manages its own state internally via `defaultValue`."},"1214":{"id":"/docs/components/segmented-controller-23","page_id":"/docs/components/segmented-controller","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/segmented-controller#controlled","content":"Use `value` and `onSelectionChange` to fully control the selected segment from parent state."},"1215":{"id":"/docs/components/segmented-controller-24","page_id":"/docs/components/segmented-controller","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/segmented-controller#sizes","content":"Three sizes are available: `sm`, `md` (default), and `lg`."},"1216":{"id":"/docs/components/segmented-controller-25","page_id":"/docs/components/segmented-controller","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/segmented-controller#icon--text","content":"Segments can include an `Icon` alongside text for added visual context."},"1217":{"id":"/docs/components/segmented-controller-26","page_id":"/docs/components/segmented-controller","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/segmented-controller#icon-only","content":"For compact layouts, segments can contain only icons. Provide an `aria-label` on each item so screen readers can identify the action."},"1218":{"id":"/docs/components/segmented-controller-27","page_id":"/docs/components/segmented-controller","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/segmented-controller#overflow","content":"When the number of options exceeds the width of the container, the component automatically shows scroll buttons to let users navigate. Users can also scroll horizontally to navigate the options."},"1219":{"id":"/docs/components/segmented-controller-28","page_id":"/docs/components/segmented-controller","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/segmented-controller#rtl-direction","content":"The segmented controller follows the current layout direction (LTR or RTL), detected automatically from the browser or system settings."},"1220":{"id":"/docs/components/segmented-controller-29","page_id":"/docs/components/segmented-controller","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/segmented-controller#disabled-states","content":"Disable the entire group with `isDisabled` on the container, or disable individual segments with `isDisabled` on specific items."},"1221":{"id":"/docs/components/segmented-controller-30","page_id":"/docs/components/segmented-controller","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/segmented-controller#data-attributes","content":"Components automatically add data attributes for styling different states:"},"1222":{"id":"/docs/components/segmented-controller-31","page_id":"/docs/components/segmented-controller","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/segmented-controller#data-attributes","content":"**SegmentedController Container:** `data-disabled`"},"1223":{"id":"/docs/components/segmented-controller-32","page_id":"/docs/components/segmented-controller","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/segmented-controller#data-attributes","content":"**SegmentedControllerItem:** `data-selected`, `data-hovered`, `data-pressed`, `data-focus-visible`, `data-disabled`"},"1224":{"id":"/docs/components/segmented-controller-33","page_id":"/docs/components/segmented-controller","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/segmented-controller#keyboard-navigation","content":"**Tab**: Moves focus to/from the segmented controller"},"1225":{"id":"/docs/components/segmented-controller-34","page_id":"/docs/components/segmented-controller","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/segmented-controller#keyboard-navigation","content":"**Arrow Left/Right**: Move to next/previous segment"},"1226":{"id":"/docs/components/segmented-controller-35","page_id":"/docs/components/segmented-controller","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/segmented-controller#keyboard-navigation","content":"**Space/Enter**: Select the focused segment"},"1227":{"id":"/docs/components/segmented-controller-36","page_id":"/docs/components/segmented-controller","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/segmented-controller#aria-support","content":"`role=\"radiogroup\"` on the container"},"1228":{"id":"/docs/components/segmented-controller-37","page_id":"/docs/components/segmented-controller","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/segmented-controller#aria-support","content":"`role=\"radio\"` on each segment"},"1229":{"id":"/docs/components/segmented-controller-38","page_id":"/docs/components/segmented-controller","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/segmented-controller#aria-support","content":"`aria-checked` indicates selection state"},"1230":{"id":"/docs/components/segmented-controller-39","page_id":"/docs/components/segmented-controller","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/segmented-controller#aria-support","content":"`aria-disabled` for disabled segments"},"1231":{"id":"/docs/components/segmented-controller-40","page_id":"/docs/components/segmented-controller","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/segmented-controller#aria-support","content":"`aria-label` required on the container for screen readers"},"1232":{"id":"/docs/components/segmented-controller-41","page_id":"/docs/components/segmented-controller","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/segmented-controller#when-to-use-a-segmented-controller","content":"When switching between 2-5 related views within the same context"},"1233":{"id":"/docs/components/segmented-controller-42","page_id":"/docs/components/segmented-controller","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/segmented-controller#when-to-use-a-segmented-controller","content":"When all options should be visible at once"},"1234":{"id":"/docs/components/segmented-controller-43","page_id":"/docs/components/segmented-controller","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/segmented-controller#when-to-use-a-segmented-controller","content":"When the selection immediately changes the displayed content"},"1235":{"id":"/docs/components/segmented-controller-44","page_id":"/docs/components/segmented-controller","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/segmented-controller#when-not-to-use","content":"For more than 5 options (use Tabs or Select instead)"},"1236":{"id":"/docs/components/segmented-controller-45","page_id":"/docs/components/segmented-controller","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/segmented-controller#when-not-to-use","content":"For form input (use RadioGroup instead)"},"1237":{"id":"/docs/components/select","page_id":"/docs/components/select","type":"page","content":"Select","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Components"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/select"},"1238":{"id":"/docs/components/select-0","page_id":"/docs/components/select","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/select","content":"Select is a dropdown for picking one or more values from a list of options. It renders a labeled trigger and a popover listbox, supports single and multiple selection, and submits naturally inside a form."},"1239":{"id":"/docs/components/select-1","page_id":"/docs/components/select","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/select#features","content":"Features"},"1240":{"id":"/docs/components/select-2","page_id":"/docs/components/select","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/select#installation","content":"Installation"},"1241":{"id":"/docs/components/select-3","page_id":"/docs/components/select","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/select#examples","content":"Examples"},"1242":{"id":"/docs/components/select-4","page_id":"/docs/components/select","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/select#default","content":"Default"},"1243":{"id":"/docs/components/select-5","page_id":"/docs/components/select","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/select#controlled","content":"Controlled"},"1244":{"id":"/docs/components/select-6","page_id":"/docs/components/select","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/select#multiple","content":"Multiple"},"1245":{"id":"/docs/components/select-7","page_id":"/docs/components/select","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/select#invalid","content":"Invalid"},"1246":{"id":"/docs/components/select-8","page_id":"/docs/components/select","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/select#disabled","content":"Disabled"},"1247":{"id":"/docs/components/select-9","page_id":"/docs/components/select","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/select#form","content":"Form"},"1248":{"id":"/docs/components/select-10","page_id":"/docs/components/select","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/select#sizes","content":"Sizes"},"1249":{"id":"/docs/components/select-11","page_id":"/docs/components/select","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/select#composed","content":"Composed"},"1250":{"id":"/docs/components/select-12","page_id":"/docs/components/select","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/select#props","content":"Props"},"1251":{"id":"/docs/components/select-13","page_id":"/docs/components/select","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/select#select","content":"Select"},"1252":{"id":"/docs/components/select-14","page_id":"/docs/components/select","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/select#selectoptions","content":"SelectOptions"},"1253":{"id":"/docs/components/select-15","page_id":"/docs/components/select","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/select#selectvalue","content":"SelectValue"},"1254":{"id":"/docs/components/select-16","page_id":"/docs/components/select","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/select#selectitem","content":"SelectItem"},"1255":{"id":"/docs/components/select-17","page_id":"/docs/components/select","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/select#features","content":"**Composable interior**: Compose `Label`, a `Button slot=\"trigger\"`, `SelectOptions`, and optional `Text` / `FieldError`. Nothing is added for you, and what you write keeps the order you wrote it in"},"1256":{"id":"/docs/components/select-18","page_id":"/docs/components/select","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/select#features","content":"**Trigger and options**: An empty `Button slot=\"trigger\"` renders the selected value and a chevron from the field. `SelectOptions` is the list in the popover the Select opens: it takes `L