d","content":"Disable a section while keeping the remaining sections available."},"1417":{"id":"/docs/components/tabs-27","page_id":"/docs/components/tabs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/tabs#manilla","content":"Use the folder-style Manilla treatment for document-oriented sections."},"1418":{"id":"/docs/components/tabs-28","page_id":"/docs/components/tabs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/tabs#overflow","content":"When the tab strip is narrower than its content, the group adds controls that move one tab at a time."},"1419":{"id":"/docs/components/tabs-29","page_id":"/docs/components/tabs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/tabs#rtl","content":"Overflow controls follow the logical reading direction."},"1420":{"id":"/docs/components/tabs-30","page_id":"/docs/components/tabs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/tabs#accessibility","content":"Tabs require an accessible label on `TabList`. Use the keyboard to move between tabs with the arrow keys. Disabled tabs are skipped. Use `keyboardActivation=\"manual\"` when focus should move independently of selection."},"1421":{"id":"/docs/components/tabs-31","page_id":"/docs/components/tabs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/tabs#accessibility","content":"`overflowLabels` is optional and defaults to \"Previous tabs\" and \"Next tabs\". Provide localized labels when needed; they should describe the logical direction rather than physical directions like \"left\" or \"right\", as the component automatically handles RTL layouts."},"1422":{"id":"/docs/components/tabs-32","page_id":"/docs/components/tabs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/tabs#accessibility","content":"`TabList` must be rendered inside `Tabs` and must provide `aria-label` or `aria-labelledby`. Give each `Tab` and its corresponding `TabPanel` the same `id`; React Aria uses that key to build their accessible relationship."},"1423":{"id":"/docs/components/tabs-33","page_id":"/docs/components/tabs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/tabs#customization","content":"The component exposes state through data attributes:"},"1424":{"id":"/docs/components/tabs-34","page_id":"/docs/components/tabs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/tabs#customization","content":"`Tabs`: `data-design=\"underline\"` or `data-design=\"manilla\"`."},"1425":{"id":"/docs/components/tabs-35","page_id":"/docs/components/tabs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/tabs#customization","content":"`Tab`: `data-selected`, `data-hovered`, `data-pressed`, `data-focus-visible`, and `data-disabled`."},"1426":{"id":"/docs/components/tabs-36","page_id":"/docs/components/tabs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/tabs#customization","content":"`TabPanel`: `data-inert` when a force-mounted inactive panel is not interactive."},"1427":{"id":"/docs/components/tabs-37","page_id":"/docs/components/tabs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/tabs#customization","content":"Use these attributes to extend styling without replacing the accessibility behavior supplied by React Aria Components. You can also use render props in `className` to style based on state (e.g., `className={({ isSelected }) => isSelected ? 'active' : ''}`)."},"1428":{"id":"/docs/components/tabs-38","page_id":"/docs/components/tabs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/tabs#customization","content":"Use `TabList`'s `containerProps` to customize the outer tab list shell, such as increasing its width."},"1429":{"id":"/docs/components/tabs-39","page_id":"/docs/components/tabs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/tabs#best-practices","content":"Use Tabs for peer panels on the same page and URL."},"1430":{"id":"/docs/components/tabs-40","page_id":"/docs/components/tabs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/tabs#best-practices","content":"Keep the number of tabs small enough for users to understand the available sections."},"1431":{"id":"/docs/components/tabs-41","page_id":"/docs/components/tabs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/tabs#best-practices","content":"Do not use Tabs for primary application navigation or route changes."},"1432":{"id":"/docs/components/tabs-42","page_id":"/docs/components/tabs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/tabs#best-practices","content":"Do not render a standalone `Tab`; compose it inside `Tabs` and `TabList`."},"1433":{"id":"/docs/components/tag","page_id":"/docs/components/tag","type":"page","content":"Tag","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Components"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/tag"},"1434":{"id":"/docs/components/tag-0","page_id":"/docs/components/tag","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/tag","content":"Non-interactive labels that highlight statuses and categories."},"1435":{"id":"/docs/components/tag-1","page_id":"/docs/components/tag","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/tag#installation","content":"Installation"},"1436":{"id":"/docs/components/tag-2","page_id":"/docs/components/tag","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/tag#examples","content":"Examples"},"1437":{"id":"/docs/components/tag-3","page_id":"/docs/components/tag","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/tag#default","content":"Default"},"1438":{"id":"/docs/components/tag-4","page_id":"/docs/components/tag","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/tag#emphasis","content":"Emphasis"},"1439":{"id":"/docs/components/tag-5","page_id":"/docs/components/tag","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/tag#sizes","content":"Sizes"},"1440":{"id":"/docs/components/tag-6","page_id":"/docs/components/tag","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/tag#inline","content":"Inline"},"1441":{"id":"/docs/components/tag-7","page_id":"/docs/components/tag","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/tag#high-contrast","content":"High Contrast"},"1442":{"id":"/docs/components/tag-8","page_id":"/docs/components/tag","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/tag#with-icon","content":"With Icon"},"1443":{"id":"/docs/components/tag-9","page_id":"/docs/components/tag","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/tag#indicator","content":"Indicator"},"1444":{"id":"/docs/components/tag-10","page_id":"/docs/components/tag","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/tag#accessibility","content":"Accessibility"},"1445":{"id":"/docs/components/tag-11","page_id":"/docs/components/tag","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/tag#screen-readers","content":"Screen readers"},"1446":{"id":"/docs/components/tag-12","page_id":"/docs/components/tag","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/tag#decorative-icons","content":"Decorative icons"},"1447":{"id":"/docs/components/tag-13","page_id":"/docs/components/tag","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/tag#indicator-dot","content":"Indicator dot"},"1448":{"id":"/docs/components/tag-14","page_id":"/docs/components/tag","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/tag#best-practices","content":"Best Practices"},"1449":{"id":"/docs/components/tag-15","page_id":"/docs/components/tag","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/tag#when-to-use","content":"When to Use"},"1450":{"id":"/docs/components/tag-16","page_id":"/docs/components/tag","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/tag#when-not-to-use","content":"When Not to Use"},"1451":{"id":"/docs/components/tag-17","page_id":"/docs/components/tag","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/tag#props","content":"Props"},"1452":{"id":"/docs/components/tag-18","page_id":"/docs/components/tag","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/tag#tag","content":"Tag"},"1453":{"id":"/docs/components/tag-19","page_id":"/docs/components/tag","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/tag#default","content":"A minimal tag with the default emphasis and size."},"1454":{"id":"/docs/components/tag-20","page_id":"/docs/components/tag","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/tag#emphasis","content":"Nine emphasis options are available. Choose the one that fits the visual tone of your context."},"1455":{"id":"/docs/components/tag-21","page_id":"/docs/components/tag","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/tag#sizes","content":"Choose a size that fits the surrounding content. Smaller tags work well in compact layouts like tables; larger tags suit headings or hero sections."},"1456":{"id":"/docs/components/tag-22","page_id":"/docs/components/tag","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/tag#inline","content":"Use `design=\"inline\"` to embed a tag within a sentence. The background and border are removed so the tag blends into the text flow."},"1457":{"id":"/docs/components/tag-23","page_id":"/docs/components/tag","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/tag#high-contrast","content":"A bolder color treatment for when tags need to stand out more - for example, on colored backgrounds."},"1458":{"id":"/docs/components/tag-24","page_id":"/docs/components/tag","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/tag#with-icon","content":"Icons reinforce the tag's meaning at a glance. Add an `Icon` as a child - it inherits the tag's color and scales with its size."},"1459":{"id":"/docs/components/tag-25","page_id":"/docs/components/tag","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/tag#indicator","content":"A minimal style that pairs a small colored dot with a neutral background. Well suited for dense layouts like tables or dashboards where multiple tags in close proximity would otherwise compete for attention."},"1460":{"id":"/docs/components/tag-26","page_id":"/docs/components/tag","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/tag#screen-readers","content":"Tags are `<span>` elements with no special ARIA role. Screen readers announce the tag's text as part of normal page content — no extra markup is needed."},"1461":{"id":"/docs/components/tag-27","page_id":"/docs/components/tag","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/tag#decorative-icons","content":"Icons passed as children must include `aria-hidden=\"true\"` so they are skipped by screen readers. The text label is the sole carrier of meaning."},"1462":{"id":"/docs/components/tag-28","page_id":"/docs/components/tag","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/tag#indicator-dot","content":"The colored dot is decorative and invisible to screen readers. The text label must convey the status on its own — never rely on the dot alone to communicate meaning."},"1463":{"id":"/docs/components/tag-29","page_id":"/docs/components/tag","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/tag#best-practices","content":"Use the indicator style in dense layouts like tables and dashboards. Use the filled style when the tag is a prominent, standalone element on a card or hero section."},"1464":{"id":"/docs/components/tag-30","page_id":"/docs/components/tag","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/tag#best-practices","content":"Default to the small size in compact layouts like tables and lists. Use medium or large only when the tag needs to stand out as a primary piece of information."},"1465":{"id":"/docs/components/tag-31","page_id":"/docs/components/tag","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/tag#best-practices","content":"Use the inline design only within running prose. In grouped or standalone contexts, the filled style provides better visual separation."},"1466":{"id":"/docs/components/tag-32","page_id":"/docs/components/tag","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/tag#best-practices","content":"Do not stack multiple tags of different emphasis on the same item. Choose the most important one — too many competing labels lose their meaning."},"1467":{"id":"/docs/components/tag-33","page_id":"/docs/components/tag","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/tag#when-to-use","content":"Showing the status of an item on a card, table row, or list entry (e.g. \"Active\", \"Expired\", \"Pending\")"},"1468":{"id":"/docs/components/tag-34","page_id":"/docs/components/tag","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/tag#when-to-use","content":"Categorizing or grouping content so users can scan and filter quickly (e.g. \"New\", \"Sale\", \"Beta\")"},"1469":{"id":"/docs/components/tag-35","page_id":"/docs/components/tag","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/tag#when-to-use","content":"Surfacing metadata about an item (e.g. \"Pro\", \"Free trial\", \"Internal\")"},"1470":{"id":"/docs/components/tag-36","page_id":"/docs/components/tag","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/tag#when-to-use","content":"Communicating priority or category in project management and collaboration tools (e.g. \"High priority\", \"In review\")"},"1471":{"id":"/docs/components/tag-37","page_id":"/docs/components/tag","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/tag#when-not-to-use","content":"If users need to click or dismiss it — use a **Button** instead."},"1472":{"id":"/docs/components/tag-38","page_id":"/docs/components/tag","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/tag#when-not-to-use","content":"If the label is part of a sentence with no visual distinction — just use text."},"1473":{"id":"/docs/components/text","page_id":"/docs/components/text","type":"page","content":"Text","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Components"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/text"},"1474":{"id":"/docs/components/text-0","page_id":"/docs/components/text","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/text","content":"Text component for displaying and formatting text content with alignment and truncation options"},"1475":{"id":"/docs/components/text-1","page_id":"/docs/components/text","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/text#features","content":"Features"},"1476":{"id":"/docs/components/text-2","page_id":"/docs/components/text","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/text#installation","content":"Installation"},"1477":{"id":"/docs/components/text-3","page_id":"/docs/components/text","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/text#examples","content":"Examples"},"1478":{"id":"/docs/components/text-4","page_id":"/docs/components/text","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/text#default","content":"Default"},"1479":{"id":"/docs/components/text-5","page_id":"/docs/components/text","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/text#as","content":"As"},"1480":{"id":"/docs/components/text-6","page_id":"/docs/components/text","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/text#align","content":"Align"},"1481":{"id":"/docs/components/text-7","page_id":"/docs/components/text","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/text#max-lines","content":"Max Lines"},"1482":{"id":"/docs/components/text-8","page_id":"/docs/components/text","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/text#wrap","content":"Wrap"},"1483":{"id":"/docs/components/text-9","page_id":"/docs/components/text","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/text#treatments","content":"Treatments"},"1484":{"id":"/docs/components/text-10","page_id":"/docs/components/text","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/text#customization","content":"Customization"},"1485":{"id":"/docs/components/text-11","page_id":"/docs/components/text","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/text#props","content":"Props"},"1486":{"id":"/docs/components/text-12","page_id":"/docs/components/text","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/text#text","content":"Text"},"1487":{"id":"/docs/components/text-13","page_id":"/docs/components/text","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/text#detail","content":"Detail"},"1488":{"id":"/docs/components/text-14","page_id":"/docs/components/text","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/text#features","content":"`Text` supplies body typography; `Detail` supplies supporting-copy typography."},"1489":{"id":"/docs/components/text-15","page_id":"/docs/components/text","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/text#features","content":"Both consume interface size and owning slot defaults. Explicit `size` and `emphasis` win independently."},"1490":{"id":"/docs/components/text-16","page_id":"/docs/components/text","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/text#features","content":"Six tiers: `xs`, `sm`, `md`, `lg`, `xl`, and `2xl`. Standalone defaults to `md`."},"1491":{"id":"/docs/components/text-17","page_id":"/docs/components/text","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/text#features","content":"`emphasis` changes feedback color; omission inherits color, including on Detail."},"1492":{"id":"/docs/components/text-18","page_id":"/docs/components/text","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/text#features","content":"`as=\"strong\"` and `as=\"em\"` provide semantic emphasis. There is no weight prop."},"1493":{"id":"/docs/components/text-19","page_id":"/docs/components/text","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/text#features","content":"Inside Button, Text preserves the full label treatment; wrapping, truncation, or color do not reset fonts."},"1494":{"id":"/docs/components/text-20","page_id":"/docs/components/text","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/text#default","content":"Basic text content."},"1495":{"id":"/docs/components/text-21","page_id":"/docs/components/text","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/text#as","content":"Setting the `as` prop allows you to change the HTML tag of the `Text` component."},"1496":{"id":"/docs/components/text-22","page_id":"/docs/components/text","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/text#align","content":"Setting the `align` prop allows you to change the alignment of the text. Choose from `start`, `center`, `end`, or `justify`; the logical keywords support RTL languages."},"1497":{"id":"/docs/components/text-23","page_id":"/docs/components/text","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/text#max-lines","content":"Setting the `maxLines` prop limits the number of displayed lines using an ellipsis."},"1498":{"id":"/docs/components/text-24","page_id":"/docs/components/text","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/text#wrap","content":"Setting the `wrap` prop controls text wrapping with values such as `wrap`, `nowrap`, `balance`, `pretty`, or `stable`."},"1499":{"id":"/docs/components/text-25","page_id":"/docs/components/text","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/text#treatments","content":"Six fixed tiers across body, supporting copy, headings, and form labels."},"1500":{"id":"/docs/components/text-26","page_id":"/docs/components/text","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/text#customization","content":"Body and Detail read the `--font-body-*` and `--font-detail-*` token families: `family`,\n`weight`, `line-height`, `variation`, and `size-{xs,sm,md,lg,xl,2xl}`. Tokens select\nvalues without changing the meaning of a tier in smaller scopes. Feedback colors use existing\n`--color-feedback-{emphasis}-text` tokens where available, with legacy-intent and literal fallbacks.\nPremium, internal, and neutral use their existing legacy feedback intents directly."},"1501":{"id":"/docs/components/text-area","page_id":"/docs/components/text-area","type":"page","content":"TextArea","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Components"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/text-area"},"1502":{"id":"/docs/components/text-area-0","page_id":"/docs/components/text-area","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/text-area","content":"Multiline text control for use inside a field."},"1503":{"id":"/docs/components/text-area-1","page_id":"/docs/components/text-area","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/text-area#installation","content":"Installation"},"1504":{"id":"/docs/components/text-area-2","page_id":"/docs/components/text-area","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/text-area#examples","content":"Examples"},"1505":{"id":"/docs/components/text-area-3","page_id":"/docs/components/text-area","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/text-area#default","content":"Default"},"1506":{"id":"/docs/components/text-area-4","page_id":"/docs/components/text-area","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/text-area#props","content":"Props"},"1507":{"id":"/docs/components/text-area-5","page_id":"/docs/components/text-area","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/text-area#textarea","content":"TextArea"},"1508":{"id":"/docs/components/text-area-6","page_id":"/docs/components/text-area","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/text-area","content":"`TextArea` is the multiline control inside a field, not a field on its own. Prefer `TextField` as the parent; see that component for fuller examples."},"1509":{"id":"/docs/components/text-area-7","page_id":"/docs/components/text-area","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/text-area#default","content":"TextArea inside TextField."},"1510":{"id":"/docs/components/text-field","page_id":"/docs/components/text-field","type":"page","content":"TextField","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Components"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/text-field"},"1511":{"id":"/docs/components/text-field-0","page_id":"/docs/components/text-field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/text-field","content":"TextField is a composed single-line or multiline text input. Use it in forms for short answers (email, search, name) or longer content (comments)."},"1512":{"id":"/docs/components/text-field-1","page_id":"/docs/components/text-field","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/text-field#features","content":"Features"},"1513":{"id":"/docs/components/text-field-2","page_id":"/docs/components/text-field","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/text-field#installation","content":"Installation"},"1514":{"id":"/docs/components/text-field-3","page_id":"/docs/components/text-field","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/text-field#examples","content":"Examples"},"1515":{"id":"/docs/components/text-field-4","page_id":"/docs/components/text-field","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/text-field#default","content":"Default"},"1516":{"id":"/docs/components/text-field-5","page_id":"/docs/components/text-field","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/text-field#controlled","content":"Controlled"},"1517":{"id":"/docs/components/text-field-6","page_id":"/docs/components/text-field","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/text-field#invalid","content":"Invalid"},"1518":{"id":"/docs/components/text-field-7","page_id":"/docs/components/text-field","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/text-field#disabled","content":"Disabled"},"1519":{"id":"/docs/components/text-field-8","page_id":"/docs/components/text-field","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/text-field#adornments","content":"Adornments"},"1520":{"id":"/docs/components/text-field-9","page_id":"/docs/components/text-field","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/text-field#multiline","content":"Multiline"},"1521":{"id":"/docs/components/text-field-10","page_id":"/docs/components/text-field","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/text-field#sizes","content":"Sizes"},"1522":{"id":"/docs/components/text-field-11","page_id":"/docs/components/text-field","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/text-field#controls-and-icons","content":"Controls and icons"},"1523":{"id":"/docs/components/text-field-12","page_id":"/docs/components/text-field","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/text-field#telephone-field","content":"Telephone Field"},"1524":{"id":"/docs/components/text-field-13","page_id":"/docs/components/text-field","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/text-field#sizing-and-typography","content":"Sizing and typography"},"1525":{"id":"/docs/components/text-field-14","page_id":"/docs/components/text-field","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/text-field#props","content":"Props"},"1526":{"id":"/docs/components/text-field-15","page_id":"/docs/components/text-field","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/text-field#textfield","content":"TextField"},"1527":{"id":"/docs/components/text-field-16","page_id":"/docs/components/text-field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/text-field#features","content":"**Composable interior**: Compose `Label`, `Input` or `TextArea`, `Text slot=\"description\"`, and `FieldError`. Omitting `Group` leaves the control as a direct field child with box chrome. Use an explicit `Group` for controls or adornments"},"1528":{"id":"/docs/components/text-field-17","page_id":"/docs/components/text-field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/text-field#features","content":"**Adornments**: Fixed text or icons before or after the input (e.g. `$`, `.00`, `px`) are composed inside `Group`, positioned by source order"},"1529":{"id":"/docs/components/text-field-18","page_id":"/docs/components/text-field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/text-field#features","content":"**Controls**: A `Button slot=\"control\"` beside the input is an interactive affix; it picks up field chrome from context"},"1530":{"id":"/docs/components/text-field-19","page_id":"/docs/components/text-field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/text-field#features","content":"**Controlled or uncontrolled**: Use `value` and `onChange` for controlled state, or `defaultValue` for uncontrolled"},"1531":{"id":"/docs/components/text-field-20","page_id":"/docs/components/text-field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/text-field#features","content":"**Multiline**: Compose a `TextArea` instead of an `Input` for multiline entry"},"1532":{"id":"/docs/components/text-field-21","page_id":"/docs/components/text-field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/text-field#features","content":"**Validation states**: Use `isInvalid` with a `FieldError` and `isDisabled` for validation and disabled state"},"1533":{"id":"/docs/components/text-field-22","page_id":"/docs/components/text-field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/text-field#default","content":"Minimal usage: a `Label` and an `Input`."},"1534":{"id":"/docs/components/text-field-23","page_id":"/docs/components/text-field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/text-field#controlled","content":"Use `value` and `onChange` for controlled state."},"1535":{"id":"/docs/components/text-field-24","page_id":"/docs/components/text-field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/text-field#invalid","content":"Use `isInvalid` with a `FieldError` for validation feedback."},"1536":{"id":"/docs/components/text-field-25","page_id":"/docs/components/text-field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/text-field#disabled","content":"Use `isDisabled` to prevent input."},"1537":{"id":"/docs/components/text-field-26","page_id":"/docs/components/text-field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/text-field#adornments","content":"Fixed text before and after the input, such as currency. Leading and trailing content is\ncomposed inside the `Group` and its position comes from source order."},"1538":{"id":"/docs/components/text-field-27","page_id":"/docs/components/text-field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/text-field#multiline","content":"Compose a `TextArea` instead of an `Input` for multiline entry."},"1539":{"id":"/docs/components/text-field-28","page_id":"/docs/components/text-field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/text-field#sizes","content":"Compare the supported `sm`, `md`, and `lg` visual sizes, plain and with an icon plus control button.\nSet `size` on `TextField` so the input and `Button slot=\"control\"` share the same size."},"1540":{"id":"/docs/components/text-field-29","page_id":"/docs/components/text-field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/text-field#controls-and-icons","content":"Put a control or an icon beside the input. A `Button slot=\"control\"` is an\ninteractive affix; static content is wrapped in a `Flex as=\"span\"` to center it and give it a gutter."},"1541":{"id":"/docs/components/text-field-30","page_id":"/docs/components/text-field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/text-field#telephone-field","content":"Compose a telephone number input paired with a country-code select."},"1542":{"id":"/docs/components/text-field-31","page_id":"/docs/components/text-field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/text-field#sizing-and-typography","content":"TextField consumes explicit size, then interface size, then `md`, and provides that size to its parts.\nLabel uses the shared label treatment. Input, TextArea, and input-group icons share input typography.\nDescriptions accept Text or Detail; explicit child typography and layout props win."},"1543":{"id":"/docs/components/text-field-32","page_id":"/docs/components/text-field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/text-field#sizing-and-typography","content":"Field size"},"1544":{"id":"/docs/components/text-field-33","page_id":"/docs/components/text-field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/text-field#sizing-and-typography","content":"Label / input tier"},"1545":{"id":"/docs/components/text-field-34","page_id":"/docs/components/text-field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/text-field#sizing-and-typography","content":"Supporting Detail tier"},"1546":{"id":"/docs/components/text-field-35","page_id":"/docs/components/text-field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/text-field#sizing-and-typography","content":"Input padding"},"1547":{"id":"/docs/components/text-field-36","page_id":"/docs/components/text-field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/text-field#sizing-and-typography","content":"Minimum input height"},"1548":{"id":"/docs/components/text-field-37","page_id":"/docs/components/text-field","tags":