","content":"**Customizable axes**: Control gridlines, tick marks, axis titles, and tick formatting"},"1762":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/bar-chart-33","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/bar-chart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/chart/bar-chart#features","content":"**Custom domains**: Set explicit x and y ranges for controlled scales across multiple charts"},"1763":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/bar-chart-34","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/bar-chart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/chart/bar-chart#features","content":"**RTL support*&#x2A;: Full right-to-left layout support for international audiences &#x2A;(in development)*"},"1764":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/bar-chart-35","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/bar-chart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/chart/bar-chart#features","content":"**Accessibility ready**: Keyboard navigation, screen reader support, and semantic HTML"},"1765":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/bar-chart-36","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/bar-chart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/chart/bar-chart#features","content":"**TypeScript support**: Fully typed with comprehensive prop interfaces"},"1766":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/bar-chart-37","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/bar-chart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/chart/bar-chart#features","content":"**VisX integration**: Leverages VisX primitives for scales, axes, shapes, and responsive layout"},"1767":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/bar-chart-38","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/bar-chart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/chart/bar-chart#default","content":"You give the chart a `series` array plus `xAccessor` and `yAccessor` so it knows which field is the category and which is the value - this is the everyday setup for one set of vertical bars."},"1768":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/bar-chart-39","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/bar-chart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/chart/bar-chart#multi-series","content":"Pass more than one entry in `series` and the bars group by category, with a legend naming each series. Use it when the comparison between series matters as much as the values themselves."},"1769":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/bar-chart-40","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/bar-chart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/chart/bar-chart#horizontal-single-series","content":"`orientation=\"horizontal\"` swaps the axes: categories run down the side and values across the bottom. Reach for it when the labels are long or the chart is really a ranking."},"1770":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/bar-chart-41","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/bar-chart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/chart/bar-chart#horizontal-multi-series","content":"Grouped bars work horizontally too. With many categories the chart scrolls vertically, which is usually easier on a phone than scrolling sideways."},"1771":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/bar-chart-42","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/bar-chart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/chart/bar-chart#custom-domain","content":"`xDomain` and `yDomain` pin down exactly which categories and value range to draw. Here category `F` has no data and still gets an empty slot, and the Y range stays `[0, 40]` even though the largest bar is 30 - handy when several charts need to share a scale."},"1772":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/bar-chart-43","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/bar-chart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/chart/bar-chart#formatted-tick-marks","content":"`xTickFormat` and `yTickFormat` shape the axis labels - abbreviated dates on one axis, thousands separators on the other. The functions receive the raw accessor value, so they also cover currency, units, or percentages."},"1773":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/bar-chart-44","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/bar-chart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/chart/bar-chart#rtl-multi-series","content":"The chart follows the current layout direction, which is normally detected from the browser or system settings. In right-to-left it mirrors the axes, bars, and labels; this example forces RTL so you can see it in a left-to-right page. RTL support is still being refined - axis rendering and tick spacing in particular."},"1774":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/bar-chart-45","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/bar-chart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/chart/bar-chart#rtl-horizontal-multi-series","content":"Horizontal grouped bars in a right-to-left layout: bars grow from the right edge and the category axis moves to the right side."},"1775":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/bar-chart-46","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/bar-chart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/chart/bar-chart#spacing-and-sizing","content":"**Bar width**: 12px (1.5 grid units)"},"1776":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/bar-chart-47","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/bar-chart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/chart/bar-chart#spacing-and-sizing","content":"**Bar padding** (multi-series): 4px between bars within a group"},"1777":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/bar-chart-48","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/bar-chart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/chart/bar-chart#spacing-and-sizing","content":"**Group gap**: Minimum 24px between bar groups"},"1778":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/bar-chart-49","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/bar-chart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/chart/bar-chart#spacing-and-sizing","content":"**Border radius**: 8px on all bars"},"1779":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/bar-chart-50","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/bar-chart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/chart/bar-chart#spacing-and-sizing","content":"**Margins**: 20px top/right, 60px bottom/left for axes and labels"},"1780":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/bar-chart-51","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/bar-chart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/chart/bar-chart#responsive-behavior","content":"**Auto-sizing**: Uses VisX's `useParentSize` hook to adapt to container width"},"1781":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/bar-chart-52","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/bar-chart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/chart/bar-chart#responsive-behavior","content":"**Horizontal scrolling**: When data points exceed available width, the chart becomes horizontally scrollable"},"1782":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/bar-chart-53","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/bar-chart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/chart/bar-chart#responsive-behavior","content":"**Sticky y-axis**: The y-axis remains visible during horizontal scroll"},"1783":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/bar-chart-54","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/bar-chart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/chart/bar-chart#responsive-behavior","content":"**Minimum spacing**: Group gaps never fall below 24px, triggering scroll instead"},"1784":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/bar-chart-55","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/bar-chart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/chart/bar-chart#accessibility","content":"**Keyboard navigation**: Bar groups are keyboard accessible with `tabIndex={0}` and `role=\"group\"`"},"1785":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/bar-chart-56","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/bar-chart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/chart/bar-chart#accessibility","content":"**Screen reader support**: Semantic HTML structure with proper ARIA attributes"},"1786":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/bar-chart-57","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/bar-chart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/chart/bar-chart#accessibility","content":"**Tooltips**: Show on both hover and focus for keyboard users"},"1787":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/bar-chart-58","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/bar-chart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/chart/bar-chart#rendering-strategy","content":"The component uses VisX primitives for optimal SVG rendering:"},"1788":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/bar-chart-59","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/bar-chart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/chart/bar-chart#rendering-strategy","content":"**Scales**: VisX's `scaleBand` and `scaleLinear` for efficient coordinate mapping"},"1789":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/bar-chart-60","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/bar-chart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/chart/bar-chart#rendering-strategy","content":"**Grouped rendering**: Bars are rendered in SVG `<Group>` elements for logical organization"},"1790":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/bar-chart-61","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/bar-chart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/chart/bar-chart#rendering-strategy","content":"**Responsive sizing**: `useParentSize` hook provides efficient resize detection with debouncing (15ms)"},"1791":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/bar-chart-62","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/bar-chart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/chart/bar-chart#scrolling-strategy","content":"**Vertical charts**: Horizontal scrolling when many data points exceed container width"},"1792":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/bar-chart-63","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/bar-chart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/chart/bar-chart#scrolling-strategy","content":"**Horizontal charts**: Vertical scrolling when many categories exceed container height"},"1793":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/bar-chart-64","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/bar-chart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/chart/bar-chart#scrolling-strategy","content":"**Sticky axes**: Positioned absolutely to remain visible during scroll"},"1794":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/bar-chart-65","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/bar-chart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/chart/bar-chart#recommendations","content":"For charts with **many data points** (>20), consider enabling horizontal scroll (default behavior)"},"1795":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/bar-chart-66","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/bar-chart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/chart/bar-chart#recommendations","content":"For **horizontal bar charts**, vertical scrolling is more mobile-friendly than horizontal"},"1796":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/bar-chart-67","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/bar-chart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/chart/bar-chart#recommendations","content":"Use **custom domains** to maintain consistent scales across multiple charts"},"1797":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/bar-chart-68","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/bar-chart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/chart/bar-chart#recommendations","content":"**Tooltips** use absolute positioning and scroll-aware calculations for accurate placement"},"1798":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/bar-chart-69","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/bar-chart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/chart/bar-chart#development-status","content":"The BarChart component is in active development. Current focus areas:"},"1799":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/bar-chart-70","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/bar-chart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/chart/bar-chart#development-status","content":"✅ Single and multi-series support"},"1800":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/bar-chart-71","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/bar-chart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/chart/bar-chart#development-status","content":"✅ Vertical and horizontal orientations"},"1801":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/bar-chart-72","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/bar-chart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/chart/bar-chart#development-status","content":"✅ Responsive behavior with sticky axes"},"1802":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/bar-chart-73","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/bar-chart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/chart/bar-chart#development-status","content":"✅ Interactive tooltips"},"1803":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/bar-chart-74","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/bar-chart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/chart/bar-chart#development-status","content":"✅ Custom domains"},"1804":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/bar-chart-75","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/bar-chart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/chart/bar-chart#development-status","content":"✅ Design system alignment"},"1805":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/bar-chart-76","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/bar-chart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/chart/bar-chart#development-status","content":"🚧 RTL compatibility (axis rendering and spacing refinement)"},"1806":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/bar-chart-77","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/bar-chart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/chart/bar-chart#development-status","content":"🚧 Tick mark positioning improvements"},"1807":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/bar-chart-78","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/bar-chart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/chart/bar-chart#development-status","content":"🚧 Additional customization options (tick formatting, axis configuration)"},"1808":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/bar-chart-79","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/bar-chart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/chart/bar-chart#bars-not-showing","content":"If bars are not visible:"},"1809":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/bar-chart-80","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/bar-chart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/chart/bar-chart#bars-not-showing","content":"**Check data**: Ensure `series` array has data and `xAccessor`/`yAccessor` return valid values"},"1810":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/bar-chart-81","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/bar-chart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/chart/bar-chart#bars-not-showing","content":"**Check domains**: Verify `yDomain` (if set) includes your data values"},"1811":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/bar-chart-82","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/bar-chart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/chart/bar-chart#bars-not-showing","content":"**Check dimensions**: Ensure container has non-zero width and height"},"1812":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/bar-chart-83","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/bar-chart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/chart/bar-chart#tooltip-positioning-issues","content":"If tooltips appear in the wrong location:"},"1813":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/bar-chart-84","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/bar-chart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/chart/bar-chart#tooltip-positioning-issues","content":"**Check scroll position**: The component accounts for horizontal scroll automatically"},"1814":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/bar-chart-85","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/bar-chart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/chart/bar-chart#tooltip-positioning-issues","content":"**Check container**: Ensure the chart container is not transformed or positioned in a complex layout"},"1815":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/bar-chart-86","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/bar-chart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/chart/bar-chart#tooltip-positioning-issues","content":"**Verify event targets**: Tooltips use mouse event coordinates and bar group positions"},"1816":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/bar-chart-87","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/bar-chart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/chart/bar-chart#performance-issues","content":"For better performance:"},"1817":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/bar-chart-88","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/bar-chart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/chart/bar-chart#performance-issues","content":"**Limit data points**: Consider pagination or filtering for very large datasets (>100 points)"},"1818":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/bar-chart-89","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/bar-chart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/chart/bar-chart#performance-issues","content":"**Debounce resize**: The default 15ms debounce on `useParentSize` balances smoothness and performance"},"1819":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/bar-chart-90","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/bar-chart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/chart/bar-chart#performance-issues","content":"**Simplify tooltips**: If tooltips are complex, consider using simpler content or disabling them"},"1820":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/donut-chart","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/donut-chart","type":"page","content":"DonutChart","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Components","Chart"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/chart/donut-chart"},"1821":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/donut-chart-0","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/donut-chart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/chart/donut-chart","content":"Donut charts are for parts-to-whole comparison—how partial elements add up to a total—shown as a ring so a few categories are easy to compare at a glance."},"1822":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/donut-chart-1","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/donut-chart","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/chart/donut-chart#installation","content":"Installation"},"1823":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/donut-chart-2","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/donut-chart","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/chart/donut-chart#examples","content":"Examples"},"1824":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/donut-chart-3","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/donut-chart","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/chart/donut-chart#default","content":"Default"},"1825":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/donut-chart-4","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/donut-chart","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/chart/donut-chart#single-slice","content":"Single slice"},"1826":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/donut-chart-5","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/donut-chart","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/chart/donut-chart#legend-placement","content":"Legend placement"},"1827":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/donut-chart-6","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/donut-chart","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/chart/donut-chart#small-slices","content":"Small slices"},"1828":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/donut-chart-7","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/donut-chart","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/chart/donut-chart#format-value","content":"Format value"},"1829":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/donut-chart-8","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/donut-chart","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/chart/donut-chart#props","content":"Props"},"1830":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/donut-chart-9","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/donut-chart","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/chart/donut-chart#donutchart","content":"DonutChart"},"1831":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/donut-chart-10","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/donut-chart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/chart/donut-chart#default","content":"You give the chart a `data` array (`id`, `name`, `value`) and a `label` in the middle - this is the everyday setup when you want several categories on one ring and a headline number or title in the hole."},"1832":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/donut-chart-11","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/donut-chart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/chart/donut-chart#single-slice","content":"When there is only one slice, the ring is full. Add `subLabel` if you want a smaller second line under the main center text."},"1833":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/donut-chart-12","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/donut-chart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/chart/donut-chart#legend-placement","content":"Switch `legend` to `right` to sit the legend beside the donut, or `bottom` to stack it underneath. `legendLabel` is there when you want a title above the legend items."},"1834":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/donut-chart-13","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/donut-chart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/chart/donut-chart#small-slices","content":"Very thin slices can be noisy to hover. Anything at or below `smallSliceThreshold` (default `0.05` of the total) is treated as “small,” and if those slices sit next to each other on the ring, one hover opens a single tooltip that lists the whole group."},"1835":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/donut-chart-14","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/donut-chart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/chart/donut-chart#format-value","content":"Use `formatValue` when the raw numbers in the tooltip should read like money, counts with separators, or whatever your product expects. The percentage of the total still formats on its own; your function only shapes the value column."},"1836":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/gauge-chart","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/gauge-chart","type":"page","content":"Gauge Chart","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Components","Chart"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/chart/gauge-chart"},"1837":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/gauge-chart-0","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/gauge-chart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/chart/gauge-chart","content":"A visual indicator for representing a single quantitative value within a known range, rendered as a semicircle arc in continuous or segmented mode."},"1838":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/gauge-chart-1","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/gauge-chart","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/chart/gauge-chart#installation","content":"Installation"},"1839":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/gauge-chart-2","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/gauge-chart","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/chart/gauge-chart#examples","content":"Examples"},"1840":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/gauge-chart-3","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/gauge-chart","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/chart/gauge-chart#default","content":"Default"},"1841":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/gauge-chart-4","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/gauge-chart","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/chart/gauge-chart#continuous-values","content":"Continuous Values"},"1842":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/gauge-chart-5","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/gauge-chart","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/chart/gauge-chart#segmented","content":"Segmented"},"1843":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/gauge-chart-6","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/gauge-chart","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/chart/gauge-chart#with-range-labels","content":"With Range Labels"},"1844":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/gauge-chart-7","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/gauge-chart","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/chart/gauge-chart#variants","content":"Variants"},"1845":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/gauge-chart-8","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/gauge-chart","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/chart/gauge-chart#label-type","content":"Label Type"},"1846":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/gauge-chart-9","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/gauge-chart","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/chart/gauge-chart#troubleshooting","content":"Troubleshooting"},"1847":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/gauge-chart-10","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/gauge-chart","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/chart/gauge-chart#gauge-not-sizing-correctly","content":"Gauge Not Sizing Correctly"},"1848":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/gauge-chart-11","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/gauge-chart","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/chart/gauge-chart#value-out-of-range","content":"Value Out of Range"},"1849":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/gauge-chart-12","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/gauge-chart","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/chart/gauge-chart#props","content":"Props"},"1850":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/gauge-chart-13","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/gauge-chart","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/chart/gauge-chart#gaugechart","content":"GaugeChart"},"1851":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/gauge-chart-14","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/gauge-chart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/chart/gauge-chart#default","content":"A continuous gauge with a single label."},"1852":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/gauge-chart-15","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/gauge-chart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/chart/gauge-chart#continuous-values","content":"Multiple continuous gauges showing different fill percentages."},"1853":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/gauge-chart-16","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/gauge-chart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/chart/gauge-chart#segmented","content":"Segmented gauges divide the arc into discrete sections (1–5). The `value` prop selects how many segments are filled."},"1854":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/gauge-chart-17","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/gauge-chart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/chart/gauge-chart#with-range-labels","content":"Min/max labels positioned below the gauge arc at the left and right edges. Both `min` and `max` must be provided."},"1855":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/gauge-chart-18","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/gauge-chart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/chart/gauge-chart#variants","content":"Color variants convey meaning at a glance — use `success`, `warning`, or `critical` alongside descriptive text."},"1856":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/gauge-chart-19","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/gauge-chart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/chart/gauge-chart#label-type","content":"Control the font size of the primary label using `labelType`. Use `'value'` for numeric or percentage values and `'text'` for short descriptive strings."},"1857":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/gauge-chart-20","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/gauge-chart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/chart/gauge-chart#gauge-not-sizing-correctly","content":"The component uses `container-type: inline-size` and fills its parent width. Ensure the parent has a defined width:"},"1858":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/gauge-chart-21","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/gauge-chart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/chart/gauge-chart#value-out-of-range","content":"Values outside the valid range are clamped silently at runtime. For continuous mode the range is 0–100; for segmented mode the range is 0 to the segment count."},"1859":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart","type":"page","content":"LineChart","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Components","Chart"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart"},"1860":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart-0","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart","content":"Line Chart shows how something changes over time or along a continuous scale. It connects data points with lines so people can quickly spot trends, peaks, dips, and patterns."},"1861":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart-1","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart#installation","content":"Installation"},"1862":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart-2","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart#examples","content":"Examples"},"1863":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart-3","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart#default","content":"Default"},"1864":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart-4","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart#multiple-series","content":"Multiple series"},"1865":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart-5","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart#gridlines","content":"Gridlines"},"1866":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart-6","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart#titles","content":"Titles"},"1867":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart-7","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart#labels","content":"Labels"},"1868":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart-8","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart#ticks","content":"Ticks"},"1869":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart-9","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart#baselines","content":"Baselines"},"1870":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart-10","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart#legend","content":"Legend"},"1871":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart-11","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart#axis-and-tooltip-formatting","content":"Axis and tooltip formatting"},"1872":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart-12","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart#custom-accessors","content":"Custom accessors"},"1873":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart-13","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart#missing-values","content":"Missing values"},"1874":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart-14","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart#fixed-domain","content":"Fixed domain"},"1875":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart-15","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart#nice-values","content":"Nice values"},"1876":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart-16","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart#zero-included","content":"Zero included"},"1877":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart-17","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart#custom-ticks","content":"Custom ticks"},"1878":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart-18","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart#band-padding","content":"Band padding"},"1879":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart-19","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart#tooltip-disabled","content":"Tooltip disabled"},"1880":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart-20","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart#crosshair-only","content":"Crosshair only"},"1881":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart-21","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart#custom-tooltip-formatting","content":"Custom tooltip formatting"},"1882":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart-22","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart#fixed-size","content":"Fixed size"},"1883":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart-23","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart#bitcoin-price","content":"Bitcoin price"},"1884":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart-24","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart#city-temperature","content":"City temperature"},"1885":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart-25","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart#browser-usage","content":"Browser usage"},"1886":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart-26","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart#rtl","content":"RTL"},"1887":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart-27","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart#color-index","content":"Color Index"},"1888":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart-28","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart#custom-tooltip","content":"Custom Tooltip"},"1889":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart-29","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart#custom-tooltip-pair-change","content":"Custom Tooltip Pair Change"},"1890":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart-30","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart#custom-tooltip-period-comparison","content":"Custom Tooltip Period Comparison"},"1891":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart-31","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart#line-styles","content":"Line Styles"},"1892":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart-32","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart#customization","content":"Customization"},"1893":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart-33","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart#data-attributes","content":"Data Attributes"},"1894":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart-34","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart#component-customization","content":"Component Customization"},"1895":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart-35","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart#accessibility","content":"Accessibility"},"1896":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart-36","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart#aria-support","content":"ARIA Support"},"1897":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart-37","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart#best-practices","content":"Best Practices"},"1898":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart-38","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart#when-to-use-linechart","content":"When to Use LineChart"},"1899":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart-39","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart#troubleshooting","content":"Troubleshooting"},"1900":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart-40","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart#chart-not-sizing-or-empty","content":"Chart Not Sizing or Empty"},"1901":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart-41","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart#dates-not-displaying-correctly","content":"Dates Not Displaying Correctly"},"1902":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart-42","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart#tooltip-or-crosshair-not-showing","content":"Tooltip or Crosshair Not Showing"},"1903":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart-43","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart#props","content":"Props"},"1904":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart-44","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart#linechart","content":"LineChart"},"1905":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart-45","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart#default","content":"One line, a time-scale X axis, and almost nothing else configured - the everyday starting point. You give the chart a `series` array and it reads `x`/`y` from each point."},"1906":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart-46","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart#multiple-series","content":"Several lines sharing one X axis, with a legend naming each of them. Reach for this when the comparison between series is the story."},"1907":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart-47","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart#gridlines","content":"`xGridlines` and `yGridlines` add faint lines across the plot so it is easier to read a value back off an axis."},"1908":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart-48","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart#titles","content":"`xTitle` and `yTitle` label what each axis actually measures, e.g. \"Month\" and \"Temperature (°F)\"."},"1909":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart-49","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart#labels","content":"`xLabels` and `yLabels` toggle the tick labels on each axis. Turn them off for sparklines or when the surrounding UI already names the values."},"1910":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart-50","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart#ticks","content":"`xTickMarks` and `yTickMarks` draw the short lines at each tick value, which helps tie a label to its exact position on the axis."},"1911":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart-51","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart#baselines","content":"`xBaseline` and `yBaseline` control the main axis lines themselves. Dropping them gives a lighter, more editorial chart."},"1912":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart-52","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart#legend","content":"`legendPosition` puts the legend above or below the plot, or hides it with `null`. Multi-series charts get a bottom legend by default."},"1913":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart-53","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart#axis-and-tooltip-formatting","content":"`xTickFormat` and `yTickFormat` shape the axis labels - dates, currency, units, percentages - and the tooltip follows the same formatting."},"1914":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart-54","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart#custom-accessors","content":"When your data does not use `x`/`y`, point `xAccessor` and `yAccessor` at the fields it does use (here `date` and `value`) instead of reshaping the data first."},"1915":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart-55","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart#missing-values","content":"A `null` Y value breaks the line instead of drawing through the gap, so missing data reads as missing rather than as a straight interpolation."},"1916":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart-56","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart#fixed-domain","content":"`xDomain` and `yDomain` pin the visible range. Use them to keep a fixed scale, or to keep several charts comparable."},"1917":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart-57","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart#nice-values","content":"`xNice` and `yNice` round the domain out to friendlier numbers (e.g. 0.2 to 1.0), so ticks land on values people expect."},"1918":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart-58","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart#zero-included","content":"`xZero` and `yZero` stretch the domain to include zero. Worth doing when the absolute size of the values matters, not just their movement."},"1919":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart-59","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart#custom-ticks","content":"Choose the ticks yourself with `xTickValues`/`yTickValues`, or just ask for roughly how many you want with `xNumTicks`/`yNumTicks`."},"1920":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart-60","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart#band-padding","content":"`xPaddingOuter` and `yPaddingOuter` add breathing room at the ends of a band or point scale so the first and last values are not pinned to the edges."},"1921":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart-61","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart#tooltip-disabled","content":"Turn off the hover affordances entirely with `tooltip={false}`, `showCrosshair={false}`, and `showDataPoints={false}` - useful for a static or print-style chart."},"1922":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart-62","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart#crosshair-only","content":"Keep the vertical crosshair for orientation while hiding the tooltip and the data point glyphs."},"1923":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart-63","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart#custom-tooltip-formatting","content":"`tooltipValueFormatter` shapes only the tooltip values, so you can show full currency or units there while the axis stays compact."},"1924":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart-64","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart#fixed-size","content":"Pass `width` and `height` to size the chart explicitly instead of letting it fill its container."},"1925":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart-65","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart#bitcoin-price","content":"A real time series: date formatting on the X axis, currency on the Y axis, gridlines, and a nice-rounded domain."},"1926":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart-66","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart#city-temperature","content":"Several cities over the same period, with a legend and a shared time axis - the multi-series case as it usually looks in a product."},"1927":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart-67","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart#browser-usage","content":"A categorical X axis (band scale) with several series and percentage formatting, for when the X values are names rather than numbers or dates."},"1928":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart-68","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart#rtl","content":"The chart follows the current layout direction, normally detected from the browser or system settings. In right-to-left it mirrors the axes and labels; this example forces RTL so you can see it in a left-to-right page."},"1929":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart-69","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart#color-index","content":"`colorIndex` pins each series to a palette color. Any series can use any index,\nindependently — here two pairs each share an index so an actual line and its\ndashed forecast read as the same color, distinguished only by line style."},"1930":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart-70","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart#custom-tooltip","content":"`renderTooltip` lets you render a fully custom tooltip and know which curve is\nhovered. Paired series share a `colorIndex`; hovering either line shows a\ntooltip specific to that line, wrapped in the default styled popover."},"1931":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart-71","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart#custom-tooltip-pair-change","content":"`renderTooltip` example combining a pair of series. Each pair shares a `colorIndex`\n(solid actual + dashed forecast); hovering either line shows the percent change of\nthe forecast against the actual for that pair, wrapped in the default styled popover."},"1932":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart-72","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart#custom-tooltip-period-comparison","content":"`renderTooltip` example styled as a period-over-period comparison card. Paired series\n(solid current period + dashed previous period) share a `colorIndex`; hovering either\nline shows both dated values and the percent change, wrapped in the default popover."},"1933":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart-73","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart#line-styles","content":"`variant` sets each series' line style — 'solid' (default), 'dashed', or\n'dotted' — useful for distinguishing actuals from forecasts or targets. The\nlegend swatch mirrors each line's style."},"1934":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart-74","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart#data-attributes","content":"The chart root exposes data attributes that reflect prop state for styling:"},"1935":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart-75","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart#data-attributes","content":"**Chart container:** `data-width`, `data-height`, `data-x-labels`, `data-y-labels`, `data-x-labels-vertical`, `data-x-baseline`, `data-y-baseline`, `data-x-tick-marks`, `data-y-tick-marks`"},"1936":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart-76","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart#component-customization","content":"Use the `className` prop on the chart container to add or override styles:"},"1937":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart-77","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart#aria-support","content":"Provide &#x2A;*`aria-label`** to describe the chart (e.g. \"Monthly sales revenue from January to May 2024\")."},"1938":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart-78","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart#aria-support","content":"Use &#x2A;*`desc`** for a longer description rendered in the SVG `<desc>` for screen readers."},"1939":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart-79","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart#aria-support","content":"The component sets ARIA attributes on interactive and structural elements as needed."},"1940":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart-80","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart#when-to-use-linechart","content":"Use for trends over time or along a continuous scale."},"1941":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart-81","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart#when-to-use-linechart","content":"Use when comparing a few series (e.g. 2-5 lines); avoid too many overlapping lines."},"1942":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart-82","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart#when-to-use-linechart","content":"Prefer a single chart with a legend over multiple small charts when comparing the same X range."},"1943":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart-83","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart#chart-not-sizing-or-empty","content":"Ensure the chart has a non-zero size. Place it in a container with explicit dimensions or use `width` and `height`:"},"1944":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart-84","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart#dates-not-displaying-correctly","content":"Use `xType=\"time\"` when the X-axis values are Date objects:"},"1945":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart-85","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart#tooltip-or-crosshair-not-showing","content":"Ensure `tooltip`, `showCrosshair`, or `showDataPoints` are not set to `false`, and that the chart receives pointer events (e.g. no overlay blocking hover)."},"1946":{"id":"/docs/components/layout/box","page_id":"/docs/components/layout/box","type":"page","content":"Box","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Components","Layout"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/layout/box"},"1947":{"id":"/docs/components/layout/box-0","page_id":"/docs/components/layout/box","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/layout/box","content":"Polymorphic layout component providing consistent spacing, elevation, rounding, and self-alignment"},"1948":{"id":"/docs/components/layout/box-1","page_id":"/docs/components/layout/box","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/layout/box#installation","content":"Installation"},"1949":{"id":"/docs/components/layout/box-2","page_id":"/docs/components/layout/box","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/layout/box#scale-sizes","content":"Scale Sizes"},"1950":{"id":"/docs/components/layout/box-3","page_id":"/docs/components/layout/box","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/layout/box#polymorphic-as-details","content":"Polymorphic `as` details"},"1951":{"id":"/docs/components/layout/box-4","page_id":"/docs/components/layout/box","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/layout/box#examples","content":"Examples"},"1952":{"id":"/docs/components/layout/box-5","page_id":"/docs/components/layout/box","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/layout/box#padding","content":"Padding"},"1953":{"id":"/docs/components/layout/box-6","page_id":"/docs/components/layout/box","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/layout/box#elevation","content":"Elevation"},"1954":{"id":"/docs/components/layout/box-7","page_id":"/docs/components/layout/box","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/layout/box#rounding","content":"Rounding"},"1955":{"id":"/docs/components/layout/box-8","page_id":"/docs/components/layout/box","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/layout/box#polymorphic-as-prop","content":"Polymorphic as Prop"},"1956":{"id":"/docs/components/layout/box-9","page_id":"/docs/components/layout/box","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/layout/box#alignment","content":"Alignment"},"1957":{"id":"/docs/components/layout/box-10","page_id":"/docs/components/layout/box","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/layout/box#rtl-support","content":"RTL Support"},"1958":{"id":"/docs/components/layout/box-11","page_id":"/docs/components/layout/box","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/layout/box#design-tokens","content":"Design Tokens"},"1959":{"id":"/docs/components/layout/box-12","page_id":"/docs/components/layout/box","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/layout/box#props","content":"Props"},"1960":{"id":"/docs/components/layout/box-13","page_id":"/docs/components/layout/box","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/layout/box#box","content":"Box"},"1961":{"id":"/docs/components/layout/box-14","page_id":"/docs/components/layout/box","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/layout/box","content":"`Box` is a polymorphic layout component that renders as any HTML element or custom component via the `as` prop. It provides consistent spacing, elevation, rounding, and self-alignment within flex or grid containers."},"1962":{"id":"/docs/components/layout/box-15","page_id":"/docs/components/layout/box","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/layout/box","content":"**Important**: Since `Flex` and `Grid` extend `Box`, prefer them for layouts. Use `Box` only when you need a non-flex, non-grid container."},"1963":{"id":"/docs/components/layout/box-16","page_id":"/docs/components/layout/box","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/layout/box#scale-sizes","content":"The spacing props use semantic t-shirt sizes for padding, gap, and other spacing properties:"},"1964":{"id":"/docs/components/layout/box-17","page_id":"/docs/components/layout/box","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/layout/box#scale-sizes","content":"`xs` - Extra small spacing"},"1965":{"id":"/docs/components/layout/box-18","page_id":"/docs/components/layout/box","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/layout/box#scale-sizes","content":"`sm` - Small spacing"},"1966":{"id":"/docs/components/layout/box-19","page_id":"/docs/components/layout/box","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/layout/box#scale-sizes","content":"`md` - Medium spacing"},"1967":{"id":"/docs/components/layout/box-20","page_id":"/docs/components/layout/box","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/layout/box#scale-sizes","content":"`lg` - Large spacing"},"1968":{"id":"/docs/components/layout/box-21","page_id":"/docs/components/layout/box","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/layout/box#scale-sizes","content":"`xl` - Extra large spacing"},"1969":{"id":"/docs/components/layout/box-22","page_id":"/docs/components/layout/box","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/layout/box#scale-sizes","content":"`2xl` - 2x extra large spacing"},"1970":{"id":"/docs/components/layout/box-23","page_id":"/docs/components/layout/box","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/layout/box#scale-sizes","content":"Custom CSS values are also supported for edge cases."},"1971":{"id":"/docs/components/layout/box-24","page_id":"/docs/components/layout/box","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/layout/box#polymorphic-as-details","content":"**HTML Elements:** When using `as=\"button\"`, TypeScript enforces button-specific props like `type`, `disabled`, and `onClick`."},"1972":{"id":"/docs/components/layout/box-25","page_id":"/docs/components/layout/box","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/layout/box#polymorphic-as-details","content":"**Custom Components:** When using `as={MyComponent}`, Box accepts that component's props. If there's a prop name conflict, Box's props take priority."},"1973":{"id":"/docs/components/layout/box-26","page_id":"/docs/components/layout/box","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/layout/box#polymorphic-as-details","content":"**Typed Refs:** Refs are correctly typed based on the `as` value - `useRef<HTMLButtonElement>` works with `as=\"button\"`."},"1974":{"id":"/docs/components/layout/box-27","page_id":"/docs/components/layout/box","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/layout/box#padding","content":"The padding props support t-shirt sizes and CSS logical properties for RTL support."},"1975":{"id":"/docs/components/layout/box-28","page_id":"/docs/components/layout/box","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/layout/box#elevation","content":"The elevation prop adds visual depth using box-shadow."},"1976":{"id":"/docs/components/layout/box-29","page_id":"/docs/components/layout/box","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/layout/box#rounding","content":"The rounding prop sets border-radius. Use `full` for fully rounded corners."},"1977":{"id":"/docs/components/layout/box-30","page_id":"/docs/components/layout/box","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/layout/box#polymorphic-as-prop","content":"Box is fully polymorphic - the `as` prop allows rendering as any HTML element or custom component while preserving type-safe props."},"1978":{"id":"/docs/components/layout/box-31","page_id":"/docs/components/layout/box","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/layout/box#alignment","content":"Self-alignment props allow Box to position itself within flex or grid containers."},"1979":{"id":"/docs/components/layout/box-32","page_id":"/docs/components/layout/box","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/layout/box#rtl-support","content":"Box uses CSS logical properties (`padding-inline-start`, `padding-block-end`, etc.) which automatically adapt to RTL layouts. No additional configuration is needed."},"1980":{"id":"/docs/components/layout/box-33","page_id":"/docs/components/layout/box","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/layout/box#design-tokens","content":"All spacing, elevation, and rounding values are derived from the theme. If no theme is provided, default values are used. This ensures consistency across the design system."},"1981":{"id":"/docs/components/layout/grid","page_id":"/docs/components/layout/grid","type":"page","content":"Grid","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Components","Layout"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/layout/grid"},"1982":{"id":"/docs/components/layout/grid-0","page_id":"/docs/components/layout/grid","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/layout/grid","content":"Two-dimensional CSS Grid layout component for complex grid-based layouts with rows and columns"},"1983":{"id":"/docs/components/layout/grid-1","page_id":"/docs/components/layout/grid","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/layout/grid#installation","content":"Installation"},"1984":{"id":"/docs/components/layout/grid-2","page_id":"/docs/components/layout/grid","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/layout/grid#scale-sizes","content":"Scale Sizes"},"1985":{"id":"/docs/components/layout/grid-3","page_id":"/docs/components/layout/grid","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/layout/grid#examples","content":"Examples"},"1986":{"id":"/docs/components/layout/grid-4","page_id":"/docs/components/layout/grid","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/layout/grid#default","content":"Default"},"1987":{"id":"/docs/components/layout/grid-5","page_id":"/docs/components/layout/grid","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/layout/grid#columns","content":"Columns"},"1988":{"id":"/docs/components/layout/grid-6","page_id":"/docs/components/layout/grid","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/layout/grid#gap","content":"Gap"},"1989":{"id":"/docs/components/layout/grid-7","page_id":"/docs/components/layout/grid","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/layout/grid#named-areas","content":"Named Areas"},"1990":{"id":"/docs/components/layout/grid-8","page_id":"/docs/components/layout/grid","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/layout/grid#responsive-grid","content":"Responsive Grid"},"1991":{"id":"/docs/components/layout/grid-9","page_id":"/docs/components/layout/grid","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/layout/grid#alignment","content":"Alignment"},"1992":{"id":"/docs/components/layout/grid-10","page_id":"/docs/components/layout/grid","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/layout/grid#form","content":"Form"},"1993":{"id":"/docs/components/layout/grid-11","page_id":"/docs/components/layout/grid","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/layout/grid#rtl-support","content":"RTL Support"},"1994":{"id":"/docs/components/layout/grid-12","page_id":"/docs/components/layout/grid","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/layout/grid#grid-vs-flex","content":"Grid vs Flex"},"1995":{"id":"/docs/components/layout/grid-13","page_id":"/docs/components/layout/grid","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/layout/grid#props","content":"Props"},"1996":{"id":"/docs/components/layout/grid-14","page_id":"/docs/components/layout/grid","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/layout/grid#grid","content":"Grid"},"1997":{"id":"/docs/components/layout/grid-15","page_id":"/docs/components/layout/grid","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/layout/grid","content":"`Grid` is a two-dimensional CSS Grid layout component for complex grid-based layouts. It extends `Box`, inheriting all `Box` capabilities (padding, elevation, rounding, self-alignment, and polymorphic `as` prop)."},"1998":{"id":"/docs/components/layout/grid-16","page_id":"/docs/components/layout/grid","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/layout/grid","content":"**Use `Grid` when**: You need explicit two-dimensional layouts with rows and columns, named grid areas, or responsive auto-fill patterns."},"1999":{"id":"/docs/components/layout/grid-17","page_id":"/docs/components/layout/grid","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/layout/grid#scale-sizes","content":"We use the same scale sizes as the `Box` component. For more information, see the **Box component documentation**."},"2000":{"id":"/docs/components/layout/grid-18","p